; The registry every observation fixture is read against.
;
; An observation file names four vocabularies and declares none of them: the
; frame its coordinates are in, the method the shot was taken by, the fix
; quality the instrument reported, and the session it belongs to. Every one of
; them arrives from here, which is what keeps the survey domain out of the
; engine.
(project
  (label "Observation fixture")
  (globalid-namespace "https://example.org/models/observations"))

(namespace frame (description "Coordinate frames declared by this model."))
(namespace method (description "How a value was obtained."))
(namespace fix (description "Fix qualities an instrument reports."))
(namespace session (description "Field occupations: one setup, one crew, one afternoon."))
(namespace shot (description "Observation records issued by the field crew."))
(namespace retirement (description "Retirement records issued by the field crew."))

(frame frame:site (label "Site survey grid") (unit m))
